  "commit_patch_header": "From a65245e3c0cae8d885a805162fc6ee21201f6eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Hannah Lanzrath <h.lanzrath@fz-juelich.de>\nDate: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:10:18 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] Enable sensitivities for channel dependent MCT parameters\n\nSensitivities for channel dependent MCT parameters can now be requested.\nBefore, there was no way to specify the channel. Add a channel_indices\nargument to add_parameter_sensitivity: an int for axial_dispersion,\nchannel_cross_section_areas and c, and an (origin, destination) tuple for\nexchange_matrix.\n\nCore reuses other slots of the parameter ID for channels:\nEXCHANGE_MATRIX takes the destination as particle type and the origin as\nbound state, INIT_C takes the channel as reaction, and COL_DISPERSION and\nCHANNEL_CROSS_SECTION_AREAS take it as particle type. The adapter now\nwrites the channel into these slots, which replaces the fixed particle\ntype 0 for MCT COL_DISPERSION.\n\nadd_parameter_sensitivity raises if a channel dependent parameter is\nmissing its channel or component, if the channel is out of range, or if a\nchannel is given for a parameter that does not depend on one.\n\nExchange matrix and channel cross section sensitivities only work with\nCADET-Core 6 (cadet/CADET-Core#522, cadet/CADET-Core#537), so their finite\ndifference tests are skipped below CADET-Core 6. Sensitivities in channels\nthat receive exchange without exchanging back stay wrong until\ncadet/CADET-Core#791 is released."
}